# Project understanding

When work reveals a fact that later tasks must remember, or shows what engineering work should happen next, append a record to `docs/pemahaman.md` before you finish.

Record facts such as:

- What a file, package, or artifact actually is
- Where important logic lives
- Constraints and distinctions that are easy to mix up

Also record the next engineering recommendation: the concrete step that should be done next, why that step is next, and what it depends on. Name the files, classes, or protocols involved. Say what should not be done yet when that boundary matters.

When a record names a class, method, field, or other symbol from reverse-engineered code, follow `.cursor/rules/docs-sumber-kode.mdc`: link the workspace file and include a short snippet. A name alone is not enough. Put that citation in the new record. Do not edit an older record to add it.

Do not record a timeline of work. That belongs in `docs/activity_log.md`. Do not record secrets, tokens, or credentials. A recommendation states the next action. It does not retell work already finished.

Do not append a record when the only change is to Cursor rules (`.cursor/rules/`) or skills (`SKILL.md`, including `.cursor/skills/` and `.agents/skills/`). Those files are agent instructions, not project facts.

## Append only

The file only grows. Existing records are a permanent record.

- Add a new record. Never edit, delete, reorder, or redate an existing record.
- If a later finding corrects an earlier record, append a new record that states the correction. Leave the earlier record unchanged.
- When two records conflict, the newer recording timestamp wins. Compare the date first, then the clock time. A same-day record that includes a clock time is newer than a date-only record.
- Do not append a record that only repeats a fact already written and still true.
- Do not append a recommendation that repeats the newest recommendation still in force. Append a new one only when the next step changes. The newest recommendation is the one to follow.
- Write in Indonesian.
- State the fact. Do not narrate the steps that uncovered it.
- Insert the new record directly under the opening paragraphs, above older records.

## Format

The heading timestamp is the recording time in Western Indonesian Time (WIB, UTC+7), 24-hour clock, minute precision. Set it once, when the record is written. Do not backdate it, and do not change it later.

Clock times recovered for records written before this format existed are final. Do not change them again. If a future record has a date and no clock time, leave it; do not invent a time.

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm WIB — Judul topik

Fakta yang harus diingat.
```

For a next-step recommendation, use this form:

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm WIB — Rekomendasi berikut: judul singkat

Langkah engineering berikutnya, alasan urutannya, dan apa yang menjadi syaratnya.
```

If one task both changes the project and reveals a lasting fact or a new next step, append to `docs/activity_log.md` and append a new record to `docs/pemahaman.md`.
